the head of public schools for the state  of nevada says children should be back  in the classroom  she addressed the state's kovid 19 task  force today  the i-team's vanessa murphy joins us  live to tell us  exactly what was discussed  brian the superintendent says children  deserve to be  back in the classroom she believes they  will get the best education  inside schools she says that can  actually help  prevent the spread of the virus here's  why  she says teachers and staff can make  sure precautions are being taken  children wearing masks social distancing  and washing their hands  she compared the washoe school district  to the clark county school district  she says washoe which has offered  in-person classes  and distance learning as well as a  combination of the two  has had a smaller percentage of children  ages 14  and under who have contracted covid19  that  increasingly shows is that the best way  to protect teachers  and students isn't to shut schools down  is to focus on all the measures that  will keep them  and their families friends and  neighborhoods safe  outside of the classroom  the clark county school district has no  plan to bring  children physically back to schools in  the near future  the head of the cdc the american academy  of pediatrics and dr  anthony fauci support children being  physically back in the classroom and  they point to data which shows that  schools and child care centers are not  major  sources for the spread of the virus now  the superintendent was one of several  people  who addressed the kovit 19 task force  today they discussed  a variety of issues the vaccine testing  and numbers the kovid 19 numbers in  nevada  really a concern right now reporting  live vanessa murphy  8 news now
 

